(father \(Ava-kakhano for father's younger brother, Ava-kakhara for) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(father's elder brother\), whereas the mother's brother is distinguished) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(as Mawa/Kuku. Similarly, parallel cousins are equated with biological) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(siblings \(Uningnao\), whereas cross-cousins fall into distinct) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(terminological classes linked to marriageability.) Tj
